  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "At the London committer's meeting, there was a consensus that improvements to service deployment should move past incremental improvements to the default WSDL implementation and allow for entirely different service descriptions.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The first step towards this is separating the service-related interfaces used by other modules out from the default 3.0 implementation classes, with the eventual goal of a module-based approach accommodating discrete service deployment models.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
